Q. How to configure NetApp OnTap using 2 linux machine?
Ans : 
1. We need to create 2 securty group. One for linux servers and another for NetApp OnTap.
        a. Create SG for linux server. Need to allow ssh port.
        b. Create SG for NetApp OnTap. Need to allow NFS ports. (111 and another is already showing in SG)
                  (Note :- In the Ontap SG we need to add SG which we have created for server. 
2. Create 2 linux servers and add first SG and we should install the NFS package.
        dnf install -y nfs-utils
3. Now Create the NetApp OnTap FSX and add NetApp OnTap SG.
4. Go to FSX volume and clickon volume, Click on attach and run below command.
          1. Create a new directory on your EC2 instance (for example, /fsx)
              mkdir /fsx
          2. Mount your volume
              mount -t nfs svm-06e5c7559b28fe8da.fs-05412f78a5b5b81a7.fsx.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com:/vol1 /fsx 
5. If we make any changes on anyone server then it will automatic reflect to another FSX directory.

